WEBVTT

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.830
I got something!

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.290
It's pretty big!

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.590
Ragworms are tasty!

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.010
What?!

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:52.300
<b>Muromi-san on the Shore</b>

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:52.300
<b>Episode 1 
"Muromi-san on the Brink"</b>

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:13.150
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:14.940
Stay still for a second!

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.190
Hurry and get it out!

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:18.070
Okay, okay...

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.660
Be gentle.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.030
This'll be my first French kiss.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.030
What?

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.540
I was just so surprised...

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:32.040
Seein's how I couldn't be 
more hungry, I went ahead

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.380
<i>That's some accent...</i>

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.090
and took a bite, 
and there was this hook.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.550
Uh, so who are you?

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:37.630
Me?

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.170
I'm Muromi!

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:41.390
<i>You just tell me your name 
like everything's normal...</i>

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.470
<i>You look like a mermaid.</i>

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.060
<i>Your tail's a mess, though.</i>

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.350
Don't look at that.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:48.890
So who're you?

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:51.440
Mukoujima Takurou.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:52.560
Takkun!

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.560
Takkun?

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:59.570
So you're the one who caught me?

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:00.820
What'cha gonna do now?

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:02.490
It's not like I can do...

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.120
Hey, don't eat my ragworms!

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.700
Come on? What's the problem?

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.000
It's not like you'll run out.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.410
I just did!

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.970
You know, they always 
say a fish will run away

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.380
if you don't keep giving her bait.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.630
Actually, I'd kind of like 
you to go away about now.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.710
Takkun, you jerk.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.930
Come on, all my bait is gone now.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.390
I guess I'll use a lure.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:42.200
I wanted to fetch some more starfish, 
but there's not enough...

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.950
I need someone to help me.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:49.330
You too can be a star if 
you help me get starfish!

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:50.910
How was that?!

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:50.910
<i>Annoying...</i>

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.750
So what are you going to do 
with the starfish, anyway?

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:54.750
What?

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.710
You know, they're starfish...

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.670
Can you do anything?

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:03.010
I'm just a starfish.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:04.430
Uh...

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.350
Shuriken!

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:09.180
Ow...

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.020
If you had no plan, you didn't 
have to force a joke in.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.020
That must have been terrible.

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.980
I didn't think you wanted to hear more!

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.980
You know, we kind of 
do look like shuriken!

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.480
Fishing is boring, ya know?

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:17.820
Knock it off already!

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.980
Let's have fun!

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.690
How can you call someone 
else's hobby not fun?

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.530
Why not go visit someone else?

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:32.660
Oh, I got something!

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.960
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.800
My boobs fell out there! 
I can't believe you!

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:40.460
Release!

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.170
I feel violated...

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.380
I can't really get it out...

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:48.140
You're such a tease.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:49.180
How?

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:51.930
What's that, anyway?

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:52.810
This lure?

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.060
What's a lure?

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:55.730
It's fake bait.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.310
You use it to get fish to bite.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.190
I see...

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:01.860
Chomp!

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.610
Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:07.160
You knew there was a hook 
on it and you bit anyway.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.820
Are you a useless black 
bass or something?

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:14.120
I knew it was a trap and I still fell for it.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.830
I'm a failure of a woman.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.330
You're like a thirty-something who's spent

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.920
all her money on host clubs.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.550
Pull yourself together. 
You're not a kid anymore.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.420
Complaining to starfish isn't 
going to do you any good.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:24.920
Sigh.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.680
Muromi-san!

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:35.230
Takkun!

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.270
Shoo! Shoo!

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.690
He's still after me!

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:48.570
Scary! Seagulls are scary!

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:51.740
Do they see you as a small fish?

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:55.330
I-If they attack again, 
I'll shoo them away for you,

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.620
so could you get off me?

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.000
You're not lying?

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:02.290
Thank god you're a man! 
I can count on you!

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:03.800
Come on, let go!

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.260
You're pretty low on the 
food chain, I guess.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:10.090
You're cut where the birds pecked you.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.550
Want me to put on 
some antibacterial ointment?

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:14.220
Why do you have that with you?

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.730
Sometimes I get stabbed by the fishing 
hooks or fish teeth, stuff like that.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:21.560
I'm not sure if it'll work 
on a mermaid, but...

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.530
It's better than just leaving you be.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.820
Don't touch me someplace weird 
when you're rubbing it on.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.200
Put it on yourself!

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.330
Abeshi!

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.450
Yes!

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.500
Yes!

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:40.290
Yes!

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:45.550
Oh yeah, I have to thank 
you for saving me.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:47.340
Is there anything you want?

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.300
You mean repaying the guy who 
saved you, like in fairy tales?

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:51.760
Like the crane or turtle?

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.970
You're not going to take me to the 
underwater castle, Ryuuguujou, are you?

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.680
You want me to take you?

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:02.020
It really exists? The Ryuuguujou?

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:02.810
Nah, it doesn't.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.650
Of course it doesn't exist!

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:06.980
<i>Damn it, Muromi-san actually existing 
is already enough of a fairy tale.</i>

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.980
You're talking about fairy tales here!

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:08.400
<i>I just don't know what's 
going on anymore.</i>

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.780
<i>Yeah, it couldn't exist...</i>

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.620
The Ryuuguujou's been 
gone for a long time.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.450
There's only a stone memorial left now.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:18.500
So there was one!

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.910
There's a AEOM Mall nearby.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:22.880
Ryuuguujou 
Memorial

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.880
The AEOM Group's opening stores 
on the bottom of the sea?!

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.540
<i>There's a sale today!</i>

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.380
<i>How about I buy everyone 
matching swimsuits?</i>

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.470
<i>They'll be sold out of everything 
if I don't get there soon.</i>

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.260
<i>I wonder if alcohol is on sale, too?</i>

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:34.390
They seem to have urban 
development under control, too!

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.470
I don't know what's going on anymore!

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.600
Maybe I should go there again. 
It's been a while.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:43.440
That cry... Is it another seagull?!

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.660
<i>She's got a lot of predators 
to worry about.</i>

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.370
There are a lot of jellyfish here.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.370
Now there's not going 
to be any fish.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.540
I'm going numb!

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:07.630
I guess there's one.

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:09.960
Wait, Muromi-san!

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:13.050
If you're going numb, that means 
they're shooting poison into you!

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.220
Huh? Really?

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:21.640
No wonder I thought I hurt 
all over for a second there.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.440
They sure like eating.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.350
Well, their bodies are almost all stomach.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:26.900
What the hell?

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.820
So you're saying they wanted to eat me?

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:32.070
I was really starting to like that 
pleasurable pain thing going on.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:34.490
You're not affected by jellyfish 
poison, Muromi-san?

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:37.870
Hm, I guess it depends on how 
much I get hit with, but...

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:39.200
Oh yeah.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:39.200
Ow...

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:42.250
When I was all tangled up with a 
Chironex jellyfish in Okinawa,

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:45.120
I was knocking on Heaven's door in 
several ways, if you get my drift.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:50.920
Kids, do not try this at home. You will die.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.670
So it doesn't affect you, then.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:54.680
You guys are lucky.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:57.340
You can just float there and get food.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:59.890
I think you have it pretty 
easy too, though.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:03.560
Oh yeah, there were a bunch of jellyfish

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:05.690
that came to Japan not 
too long ago and it was a mess.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.610
Was that really because 
of global warming?

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.520
Do you know anything?

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:14.320
Pfft, global warming?

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.660
You hear about global warming a 
lot lately, but I'm not sure.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.910
Climate changes all the time, ya know?

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:20.780
You think so?

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.500
You know the Earth has a history of 
being destroyed and being recreated.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.790
It wasn't too long ago that the 
dinosaurs were reigning over the Earth.

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:33.170
When a meteor fell and the ice age 
came, they disappeared in an instant.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:38.470
There was a global flood, too.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:41.310
Species that couldn't adapt 
met natural selection!

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:44.180
W-Wait a second...

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:47.270
Muromi-san, you've been alive since 
the Cretaceous and Jurassic Periods?!

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:48.560
That's rude!

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.270
It's not like I wouldn't know 
the history of the Earth too.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.190
Could you not treat me like 
some middle-aged woman?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:56.450
Sorry, but does a 9-digit age 
qualify as "middle-aged"?

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:01.030
Muromi-san, who did you 
learn history from anyway?

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.660
Your mom or something?

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:03.790
Poseidon.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:07.120
So now we have the name of 
the Greek god of the sea.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.920
It's not like I know everything.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.590
I was just taught what happened 
before I was born at school.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:13.380
School?

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:16.590
You don't know what happened before 
you were born either, right?

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:20.800
Fine. I'm sorry I asked.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:23.720
So when were you born anyway, Muromi—

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.520
Jellyfish Strike!

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:29.020
<b>Jellyfish Strike!!!</b>

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:33.980
Ow!

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.690
Hmph. No manners at all.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:39.200
You shouldn't ask a woman her age.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:48.710
Fine. This guy with no manners 
will leave you be, then.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:51.330
Wait, Takkun!

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:05.640
Stop by again.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.850
Muromi-san's so difficult,

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:13.190
right?

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.110
Yeah...

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.820
We've got good weather again today.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.320
Yeah.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:25.080
Hey Takkun, I've got 
something to ask of you.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:26.040
Of me?

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:29.580
You're the only one I can 
ask stuff like this...

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.080
Well, if it's something I can do...

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:34.290
What is it?

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:36.840
I... Uh...

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:40.010
You know...

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.140
Fertilize these?

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.100
Hell no!

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:50.100
<b>To be continued...</b>

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:52.730
Takkun, are you leaving already? Don't go!

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:54.020
I want to come with you.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:54.860
Muromi-san...

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.650
I thought guys liked stuff like that?

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:57.940
No, actually it turns them off.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:58.670
That's strange.

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:01.490
That's what it said in the 
May 1752 Edition of XXX.

00:11:59.880 --> 00:13:11.000
Next Time 
"Muromi-san and the Legendary Sea Creatures"

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:02.850
They've got XXX in the sea?

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:03.490
Sure do!

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.750
All of XXX?
